{"id": "7c2b1bf0-04b8-4be2-be44-95fa69c984aa", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Let me pull together the information needed for a thorough review of your Firehose delivery streams. This spans several independent data sources (resource configs, delivery metrics, quotas), so I'll gather them in parallel.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_BRMNCBtqZUdgjtt3UHYE2m", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Perform a configuration-level operational review of all Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams in us-east-1, account 012345678901_1, covering security and reliability posture.",
  "context": "User wants a full operational review of Firehose delivery streams covering security, reliability, delivery health, performance, cost, and service quotas, with severity ratings per finding. This slice covers security and reliability configuration only (not metrics/delivery health, which is handled separately).",
  "resources": ["Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams, us-east-1, account 012345678901_1"],
  "timeframe": "current configuration state",
  "criteria": "For EACH delivery stream, use list_delivery_streams and describe_delivery_stream (boto3 service 'firehose') to capture: (1) Security: server-side encryption (SSE) enabled/disabled and key type (AWS owned vs KMS CMK), IAM role permissions scope (over-permissive wildcards), VPC delivery config for destinations that support it, TLS/HTTPS endpoint usage for HTTP endpoint destinations, resource policy / cross-account exposure. (2) Reliability: source type (direct PUT vs Kinesis Data Stream vs MSK), destination type and backup/failover configuration (S3 backup mode for non-S3 destinations - enabled/disabled, especially 'FailedOnly' vs 'AllDocuments'), error output prefixes configured, retry duration settings, buffering hints (interval/size), delivery stream status (ACTIVE/CREATING/DELETING), encryption-at-rest for backup S3 bucket. Also check CloudWatch logging enabled for error diagnostics on each stream. Flag any stream lacking S3 backup for non-S3 destinations, lacking encryption, lacking CloudWatch error logging, or using overly broad IAM roles. Rate each finding by severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low) and list the specific stream name(s) affected."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}, {"id": "tooluse_RIqUnSR0dQbLTRhNhv71uV", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Analyze CloudWatch metrics for all Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams in us-east-1, account 012345678901_1, to assess delivery health, performance, and cost efficiency.",
  "context": "User wants a full operational review of Firehose delivery streams covering security, reliability, delivery health, performance, cost, and service quotas, with severity ratings per finding. This slice covers CloudWatch metrics-derived delivery health, performance, and cost signals (not static config, which is handled separately).",
  "resources": ["Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams, us-east-1, account 012345678901_1", "AWS/Firehose CloudWatch namespace"],
  "timeframe": "now - 7d to now, with finer resolution on the most recent 24h",
  "criteria": "For EACH delivery stream, pull AWS/Firehose CloudWatch metrics: DeliveryToS3.Success / DeliveryToS3.DataFreshness, DeliveryToSplunk.Success, DeliveryToHttpEndpoint.Success, DeliveryToElasticsearch.Success (whichever apply to each stream's destination), ThrottledRecords, DataReadFromKinesisStream.Records / records in, IncomingBytes, IncomingRecords, Throughput, backpressure/limit metrics (ThrottledGetRecords, ThrottledDescribeStream for KDS source), ExecuteProcessing errors (Lambda transform failures) if applicable, and FailedConversion (for format conversion) if applicable. Identify: (1) Delivery health: any sustained Success rate below 100%, rising DataFreshness (indicating delivery lag/backlog), throttling events. (2) Performance: throughput approaching documented per-stream quotas, high data freshness latency, Lambda transformation errors/duration if used. (3) Cost: streams with very low incoming volume (candidates for consolidation or on-demand review), use of format conversion or dynamic partitioning (cost multipliers), buffering hint configuration relative to typical cost/latency tradeoffs. Rate each finding by severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low) and name the specific stream(s) and metric values/timestamps supporting it."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}, {"id": "tooluse_U3g7IPu5HKJLO4R4enTIV7", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Assess Amazon Data Firehose service quota usage in us-east-1, account 012345678901_1, versus current limits.",
  "context": "User wants a full operational review of Firehose delivery streams including service quotas, with severity ratings. This slice covers quota headroom only.",
  "resources": ["Amazon Data Firehose, us-east-1, account 012345678901_1", "Service Quotas for firehose service code"],
  "timeframe": "current",
  "criteria": "Determine the current number of delivery streams versus the account quota (default 50 per region for most destinations), and where possible the per-stream throughput quotas (e.g. records/sec, MB/sec for PUT and KDS-as-source streams) versus actual observed throughput. Use boto3 service-quotas (service code 'firehose') list_service_quotas / list_aws_default_service_quotas, cross-referenced with the actual delivery stream count from firehose list_delivery_streams. Flag any quota utilization above 70% as Medium, above 85% as High, above 95% as Critical. Report exact numbers (current usage / quota value)."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}], "created_at": null}
